---
/**
 * /okoli   Tipy na výlety.
 *
 * The page for someone who has decided the cottage looks right and now wants to
 * know what they can do from it. It answers the same question as the homepage's
 * Okolí and DolníMorava sections, but in full.
 *
 * SECTION ORDER   docs/04-pages.md §/okoli:
 *   1. PageHero
 *   2. Intro   Dolní Morava, Stezka v oblacích, Sky Bridge 721 (§7.1 rewrite)
 *   3. Regional map   the illustrated aerial photograph with full alt text
 *   4. Výlety a atrakce   the trip index, from VYLETY
 *   5. Lyžování   LYZOVANI (--jinovatka winter section, legitimately)
 *   6. Koupání   KOUPANI_BLIZKO and KOUPANI_DALSI
 *   7. CtaBand → /terminy-a-ceny
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THIS PAGE IS FIVE LISTS AND THE SHAPES HAVE TO DIFFER
 *
 * The order above is unchanged and the content is unchanged; what changed is
 * that the sections no longer all look alike. Every one of items 4, 5 and 6 is
 * "some places, with a distance on each", and each of them was rendered as
 * bordered rectangles in a grid   so the page was a photograph, a map, and then
 * three screens of near-identical boxes. There is not a single `.card` left on
 * it now. In order down the page:
 *
 *   2. a three-layer parallax stage, the copy on an opaque panel in front of it
 *        OkoliIntro.astro
 *   3. one wide plate, as big as it can be and still fit on the screen, with
 *      nothing beside it   OkoliMapa.astro
 *   4. a catalogue: name / description / figures in three columns, with the
 *      distances forming a second column of display type down the right-hand
 *      edge the way page numbers do in a contents list   OkoliVylety.astro
 *   5. a single statement   one name, two figures, one paragraph   and the six
 *      unmeasured areas as a run of names   OkoliLyzovani.astro
 *   6. two figures across the measure, then ten names in three quiet columns
 *        OkoliKoupani.astro
 *
 * Four of the six are lists of places with distances on them, so the SHAPES are
 * what keep them apart: a plate, a table, a statement, a column set. Nothing on
 * this page is boxed and there is no `.card` on it anywhere. Each component's own
 * header comment carries the argument for its shape.
 *
 * The one rule that binds them: the difference between an entry WITH a verified
 * distance and one WITHOUT is always carried by typography and position, never
 * by an invented figure and never by decoration. Three of these layouts make the
 * distance the loudest thing in the row, which means a missing one leaves a
 * visible hole   and that hole is the correct rendering. See the null rule in
 * src/data/okoli.ts.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * BAND SEQUENCE (after the dark page hero):
 *   photograph → --kamen → --omitka → --jinovatka → --kamen → --omitka
 * No two adjacent sections share a colour. Last section is light (--omitka) ✓
 * so the footer treeline (--les silhouette) rises out of it visibly.
 *
 * ⚠ The intro is now the second full-bleed photograph in a row, directly under
 * the page hero. That is deliberate and it is the one place on this site where
 * it happens: the hero is dark summer timber with type laid straight on it, the
 * intro is a lit winter snowfield with the copy on an opaque --omitka panel, and
 * the pair reads as a cover followed by an opening spread rather than as two
 * heroes. Do not add a third.
 *
 * HISTORIE A PAMÁTKY (§/okoli section 6)   NOT A SEPARATE SECTION.
 * Klášter Hedeč, Vojenské muzeum Králíky and Králíky are included in the main
 * VYLETY card grid in OkoliVylety.astro. A separate section would show the same
 * cards a second time with only a heading change. See OkoliVylety.astro for the
 * full reasoning comment.
 *
 * HERO PRELOAD PATTERN   docs/04-pages.md "PAGE HERO PRELOAD":
 * getImage() resolves the same transform that PageHero.astro renders, so the
 * browser's preload finds the exact file it will need. If they drift apart, the
 * image is downloaded twice   the worst outcome for this site's one fast image.
 */
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/sections/CtaBand.astro';
import OkoliIntro from '../components/pages/okoli/OkoliIntro.astro';
import OkoliMapa from '../components/pages/okoli/OkoliMapa.astro';
import OkoliVylety from '../components/pages/okoli/OkoliVylety.astro';
import OkoliLyzovani from '../components/pages/okoli/OkoliLyzovani.astro';
import OkoliKoupani from '../components/pages/okoli/OkoliKoupani.astro';

import { PAGE_HERO_PRELOAD_PROPS, PAGE_HERO_SIZES } from '../data/pageHero';

/*
 * Resolve the page hero transform here so <head> can preload exactly the variant
 * PageHero.astro will render. Identical props → identical output → Astro dedupes
 * the transform; this costs nothing extra in the build.
 */
const hero = await getImage(PAGE_HERO_PRELOAD_PROPS);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tipy na výlety v okolí"
  description="Co podniknout z chalupy Heřmanka: Dolní Morava a Sky Bridge 721 12 minut autem, Králický Sněžník pěšky od dveří, koupání, lyžování, historické Králíky a Klášter Hedeč."
  heroPreload={{ src: hero.src, srcset: hero.srcSet.attribute, sizes: PAGE_HERO_SIZES }}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Tipy na výlety"
    lead="Dolní Morava 12 minut autem, Králický Sněžník od dveří. Les začíná deset metrů za chalupou."
  />
  <OkoliIntro />
  <OkoliMapa />
  <OkoliVylety />
  <OkoliLyzovani />
  <OkoliKoupani />
  {/*
    CtaBand is the last section. band="omitka" so it differs from the --kamen
    OkoliKoupani above it, and stays light so the footer treeline is visible.
    href points at /terminy-a-ceny per docs/04-pages.md §/okoli item 7.
  */}
  <CtaBand
    href="/terminy-a-ceny"
    nadpis="Máte zájem o pobyt?"
    text="Zkontrolujte dostupnost termínů a napište nám počet osob. Ozveme se co nejdříve."
    cta="Zkontrolovat termíny"
    band="omitka"
  />
</BaseLayout>
